# Template System Rules

## ⚠️ **Critical: Always Run Commands in Theme Directory**
```bash
cd wp-content/themes/chairforce/
```

## Chairforce Template Structure

### **Key Directories**
- **`/templates/`** - Page layouts (index, single, archive, etc.)
- **`/parts/`** - Reusable components (header, footer, archive-filters)

## Template Files

### **Key Files**
- `index.html`, `single.html`, `page.html`, `archive.html`
- `header.html`, `footer.html`, `archive-filters-and-grid.html`

## How to Create Templates

### **Basic Structure**
```html
<!-- wp:template-part {"slug":"header","theme":"chairforce","tagName":"header","className":"site-header"} /-->
<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"main","metadata":{"name":"Main"},"className":"","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<main class="wp-block-group"><!-- Your content here --></main><!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:template-part {"slug":"footer","theme":"chairforce","tagName":"footer","className":"site-footer"} /-->
```

### **Using Patterns**
```html
<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"chairforce/hero-large"} /-->
<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"chairforce/archive-filters-and-grid"} /-->
<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"chairforce/banner-cta-find-an-expert"} /-->
```

